  "body": "Closes #1150\nClaim: cloud/i1150-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i1150-sonnet)\n\n**Problem.** Nine sheets close with a text button « Fermer » (HIG › Toolbars: use the standard close symbol, no text label); the image-upload panel puts it on the trailing (confirm) side. Legacy (`87fe0d1c`, `AnswerView.swift:1825-1848`, `MessagesView.swift:6749-6760`) uses an `xmark` symbol on the leading edge.\n\n**Cause.** Each sheet built its own `Button(\"Fermer\")`.\n\n**Change.** One shared `SheetCloseToolbarItem` (`Button(role: .close)` in `.cancellationAction`, « Fermer » kept as accessibility label, optional `isDisabled` for the poll's in-flight send) used by the nine sheets of the issue plus `ReaderPageSheet` (which had its own `xmark` button, same pass per #836). No change to the viewer's swipe-down (operator's call, #1070). `ReaderOfflineSave`'s banner button is not a sheet and is left alone.\n\n**Tests.** `SheetCloseSourceTests` (source scan, same pattern as `FloatingCardSourceTests`): no `Button(\"Fermer\"` outside the shared item (fails on the 10 pre-change sites; checked by grep with the Reader/Polls edits reverted: 4 hits, 0 after), the shared item uses `role: .close` + `.cancellationAction`, the ten sheets reference it. Not run here: Linux session cannot build the app; compile check pending.\n\nDevice check owed (Mac, #893): each sheet shows the system close symbol on the leading edge; VoiceOver reads « Fermer ».\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
