   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5, round 1)**\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5): APPROVE** — head 540637513dd98f12e2acfbf1c7ba3212b7d2a794\n\nI found nothing that blocks the merge. There are two Low findings and one Detail.\n\n1. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Common/SheetCloseSourceTests.swift:27-30`. The scan only catches `Button(\"Fermer\"`. Three regressions would pass it:\n   - `Button { dismiss() } label: { Image(systemName: \"xmark\") }` in a toolbar;\n   - `Label(\"Fermer\", …)`;\n   - a dismiss moved back to `.confirmationAction`.\n\n   The doc comment at line 4 says \"never on the confirm side\", but no test checks this for the call sites. Fix: also flag `ToolbarItem` blocks that contain `dismiss()` or `systemName: \"xmark\"` outside the shared item, or narrow the doc comment to what the test checks.\n2. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFR/Common/SheetCloseToolbarItem.swift:4`. The comment says VoiceOver \"reads the role's own title anyway\". That makes `.accessibilityLabel(\"Fermer\")` look redundant, but it is the line that guarantees « Fermer » when the system language is not French. Fix: state that reason instead.\n3. **Detail**, `SheetCloseSourceTests.swift:51`. `theNineSheetsUseTheSharedItem` lists ten files (it includes `ReaderPageSheet`). Rename it.\n\nThe call sites keep their behaviour: `PollSheet` still disabled while `.sending` (`interactiveDismissDisabled` unchanged); `FilteredPostsView` still calls `model.closeResult()`; `ImageUploadView` moves to the leading edge; `ReaderPageSheet` goes from `.topBarLeading` to `.cancellationAction`, same place; no leading-item conflict.\n\nVerified: full diff read; `swiftlint lint --strict` on the 12 changed files clean; `Button(\"Fermer\"` occurs 11 times on `origin/dev-swift` and once at the head (the exempted `ReaderOfflineSave`); an empty path walk fails both `#require` checks; Swift 6 isolation read through. Not compiled on Linux: `Button(role:action:)` (iOS 26+) is the reviewer's reading of the API.\n\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
